1
00:01:01,880 --> 00:01:05,920
Taming the Husband

2
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:08,400
Episode 17

3
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:18,600
Such a droopy, miserable flower,

4
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:21,080
and yet you love it.

5
00:01:25,080 --> 00:01:26,640
If you don't like it, Mother,

6
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:28,640
why bother with it?

7
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,080
You're such a fool.

8
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:39,840
It used to be passable,

9
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:42,000
but now that it's dyed,

10
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:44,320
it's unbearably gaudy.

11
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:46,480
Jingxing,

12
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:52,160
why keep forcing it?

13
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,080
Nobody wants it.

14
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,960
If I didn't want it,

15
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:03,840
I'd have thrown it out long ago.

16
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:06,600
It was lovely, pure and white,

17
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:08,640
but trying so hard to please

18
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,800
only spoils its beauty.

19
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:12,760
If you like it, Mother,

20
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:14,880
why not tend to it yourself?

21
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:16,960
No one used to mistreat it.

22
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:19,640
It's a demanding flower,

23
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,840
it needs loose soil,
just the right amount of water,

24
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:23,080
and so much more.

25
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:25,440
I know,

26
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:28,920
but I'll find a way
to give it what it needs.

27
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,640
Next time, next time, I promise!

28
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,040
Next time, I promise!

29
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:30,040
-Next time, I promise!
-Next time, I promise!

30
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:39,040
This is for your mother,

31
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:41,000
and together with what you've earned,

32
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:43,640
it should cover your debts.

33
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:46,600
Thank you for all your hard work.

34
00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:52,640
Two bowls of pork offal stew,

35
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:53,960
a small jug of liquor,

36
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:55,640
and a plate of sliced pig ears.

37
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:59,160
I've seen him before.

38
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:07,800
The food's not even here,

39
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:08,880
so why shut the door?

40
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:11,200
Is this some kind of bandit's den?

41
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:13,240
Do you remember me?

42
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:17,120
The authorities are cracking down,

43
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:19,640
holding up shipments,

44
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:21,400
so of course salt prices are rising!

45
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:23,440
Before salt prices even soared,

46
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:24,840
you already knew what was coming,

47
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:26,440
which is rather strange.

48
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:30,320
I just heard someone
talking about it, that's all.

49
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:31,400
Who?

50
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,560
I…

51
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:37,920
I…

52
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:45,640
Who's your contact?

53
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:50,040
Officials spread the news

54
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:52,040
and helped your uncle make a fortune.

55
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,720
So your uncle and the officials…

56
00:04:56,080 --> 00:04:57,640
That reminds me of something.

57
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:00,120
When you were held at the government hall,

58
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:02,160
officials kept me from reaching you.

59
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:03,280
And then…

60
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:04,960
Jianwei,

61
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:07,920
go and fetch our sounding crew.

62
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:10,080
I asked already.

63
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:11,560
Your uncle said the ships needed work

64
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:13,040
and borrowed every last man.

65
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:15,440
I thought the Huangs were behind it

66
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:16,840
and Uncle was just taking advantage
of the situation.

67
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:20,080
But now, it all seems too convenient.

68
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:22,920
How did he get mixed up with officials?

69
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,040
With him being so stingy,

70
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,640
how much could he pay them?

71
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:27,960
Official corruption is a serious crime,

72
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:30,640
so for our own sake and the family's,

73
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,520
we have to get to the bottom of this.

74
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:35,000
With such a tangled mess,

75
00:05:35,200 --> 00:05:36,440
where do we even start?

76
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:41,720
My lady, Master Bai sent word

77
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:43,320
that he's taken care of things

78
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:45,320
and asks to meet
at Shuyu Terrace tomorrow.

79
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:54,440
Here are the goods you wanted.

80
00:05:56,680 --> 00:06:01,280
You do know buying over the limit
can land you in prison, right?

81
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:03,640
I had to call in favors
from several of my guys

82
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:04,760
just to pull this together,

83
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:06,800
so surely that deserves something?

84
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:12,440
Those spices you brought back

85
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,880
from Yunnan and Guangdong,

86
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,320
how about sparing a little for family?

87
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:17,440
You're not her family.

88
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:19,040
Sorry about that.

89
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:30,680
Xie Chengzong's salt permit
Illegal salt sales are strictly forbidden

90
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:32,040
Bai Junmei.

91
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:34,000
-What?
-Look here.

92
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:37,240
Let me see.

93
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,040
They've erased the writing on old permits

94
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,200
and passed them off as new ones.

95
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,120
This…

96
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:45,680
Well!

97
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:48,560
The Xies really have some nerve,

98
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:50,640
-even resorting to forgery!
-Without forgeries,

99
00:06:50,760 --> 00:06:52,200
how would the officials get their cut?

100
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:53,920
You…

101
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:57,880
Do you have a death wish?

102
00:06:58,200 --> 00:06:59,960
Before we took over the salt shop,

103
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:01,360
word had already spread

104
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:02,520
that salt prices would rise.

105
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:04,120
The first buyers

106
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:05,800
were the well-informed
major salt merchants,

107
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:07,560
the hardest ones to fool,

108
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,880
so the shop must have sold them
genuine permits.

109
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:13,320
Once nearly all
the genuine permits were sold,

110
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:16,160
they hurried to alter the old ones
in the storeroom.

111
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:18,440
Then they lured
an unsuspecting Baozhu into taking over,

112
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:19,800
selling real and fake permits together.

113
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,280
…was collected with my salt permits.

114
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:23,280
The forgeries were expertly done,

115
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:24,640
and by the time she took over,

116
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:27,000
most of the permits in stock were fakes.

117
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,480
She'd never seen a genuine one,

118
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:30,360
so how could she tell them apart?

119
00:07:30,840 --> 00:07:33,840
Even if she'd never seen a real one,

120
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:36,200
surely the shop clerks had?

121
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:41,280
They were covering for their old master,

122
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:42,800
which makes sense.

123
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:14,840
Good.

124
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,960
If we're doing this,
it needs to be the best, and ours alone.

125
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:20,840
Raise the price and limit the supply

126
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:23,040
to keep them wanting more.

127
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:31,920
That poor Baozhu works herself to death
for so little money,

128
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:35,040
spending all day with those lowlifes

129
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:37,000
and not minding the stench of their sweat!

130
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,280
Then again,

131
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:42,840
the smokier things get on their end,

132
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:46,400
the better our perfumed powder sells.

133
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,240
In that case,

134
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:53,440
I owe you my thanks.

135
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:57,440
It's only my duty to help you, Mother.

136
00:08:57,760 --> 00:08:59,240
Listen to you,

137
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:01,480
making me sound so old.

138
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:06,760
By the way, did you get what I asked for?

139
00:09:10,160 --> 00:09:12,360
As for the spice proportions
and the soaking process,

140
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:15,400
I've written it all down,
exactly as they do it.

141
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:17,960
Good.

142
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:19,360
Now we just need your father

143
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,000
to get those Yunnan and Guangdong spices.

144
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:24,480
Then I'll open
a pork offal stew shop, too,

145
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:26,360
and put her out of business.

146
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:30,600
Mother.

147
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:36,040
There you are.

148
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Letter of recommendation from the Xies

149
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:40,120
Lady Jin, you can't go in!

150
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:41,200
Lady Jin!

151
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:46,800
What's wrong, Baozhu?

152
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:49,080
Don't tell me the wind died down

153
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:52,600
and that pig actually fell out of the sky?

154
00:09:56,160 --> 00:09:57,160
I need to talk to you.

155
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:01,720
Go ahead.

156
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:13,880
Pine breezes sing with the bamboo

157
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:18,280
Why?

158
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:21,040
About the letter of recommendation...

159
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:24,880
It's not that we won't give you one,

160
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:26,280
-Grandmother won't--
-You…

161
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:30,440
What about me?

162
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:34,520
Why did you let someone move my jasmine?

163
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:39,360
It was out of place.

164
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:41,160
Did it bloom too late for you,

165
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:45,560
or was the color not to your liking?

166
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:47,800
It bloomed right in season,

167
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:49,080
and it's beautiful,

168
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:51,440
it just doesn't suit my vase.

169
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:53,200
What would be right?

170
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:55,040
There are all kinds of flowers,

171
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:56,960
and I like the bright, gaudy ones,

172
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:59,040
but the others are no less lovely.

173
00:10:59,680 --> 00:11:01,040
Your jasmine is beautiful,

174
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:02,800
but in my vase,

175
00:11:03,160 --> 00:11:04,480
its branches will just droop
onto the table

176
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,760
and end up getting dirty.

177
00:11:06,320 --> 00:11:09,560
I think it deserves to hang up high,

178
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,240
soaking up the rain and sunshine,

179
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:13,000
where everyone can see it.

180
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:19,480
Fine,

181
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:22,480
I understand,

182
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,040
and that's exactly what I'm doing.

183
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:28,440
From now on, stop coming here to judge me.

184
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:30,520
You go your way, I'll go mine.

185
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:32,240
Goodbye.

186
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,960
That letter of yours,
did you get it honestly?

187
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:36,360
What if I didn't?

188
00:11:36,560 --> 00:11:37,800
You know you shouldn't have done this.

189
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:39,440
You know I had no choice!

190
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:49,040
Why are you looking at me like that?

191
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:55,120
We're the same, born low,
dependent on others,

192
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:57,680
refusing to accept our lot,
and fighting for a chance,

193
00:11:58,080 --> 00:12:01,400
so why are you standing there
looking down on me?

194
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:02,680
I want you to have a good life,

195
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:04,280
or at least…

196
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:05,560
at least a clear conscience.

197
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:07,760
What good is a clear conscience?

198
00:12:08,040 --> 00:12:10,000
People respect fine clothes, not people!

199
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:11,640
When the well-born are kind,

200
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:14,280
it's called generosity,
but when the low-born do the same,

201
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:16,000
everyone takes advantage of them,

202
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:17,560
then calls them fools!

203
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:19,640
No wonder

204
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:21,920
poverty breeds cunning,
and wealth breeds a conscience.

205
00:12:23,080 --> 00:12:26,720
And I was born in that mire,
one of those fools!

206
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:28,040
Yes,

207
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:30,640
heaven has been good to me,

208
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:32,680
showing me palaces,

209
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:35,720
but not giving me a ladder to reach them!

210
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,120
So if I made my own way up,

211
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:39,960
what have I done wrong?

212
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:43,440
You say poverty breeds cunning
and wealth breeds a conscience,

213
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:45,320
but I don't agree.

214
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:48,760
For someone poor,
the road to success is hard.

215
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:50,800
Maybe the world's too dark,

216
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:53,520
the mire too deep,
with too many wrong turns,

217
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,960
but you've made it this far,
and that alone is no small feat.

218
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:58,440
I just can't bear to watch you
go down the wrong path.

219
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:00,000
-That's why I--
-"Look out for yourself,

220
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:01,520
or heaven won't spare you."

221
00:13:03,840 --> 00:13:05,080
Then why are you upset

222
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:07,760
and trembling?

223
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:10,880
Because you know it's wrong,

224
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:12,720
and that you shouldn't take this road.

225
00:13:13,160 --> 00:13:14,800
You know the moon at the bottom of a well

226
00:13:14,920 --> 00:13:16,040
is just a pool of dirty water,

227
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:17,680
yet you're plunging right in.

228
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,880
How can I see that and do nothing?

229
00:13:20,760 --> 00:13:21,760
Song Jingxing,

230
00:13:22,240 --> 00:13:23,840
I'm not here to judge you,

231
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:25,960
because I know you're a good person

232
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:28,160
who must have been desperate
to do something like this.

233
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:29,680
I just want you to know

234
00:13:30,400 --> 00:13:33,000
you don't have to be afraid,
because you're not out of options,

235
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:35,560
not when you have me and Xie Yan.

236
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:37,400
Could you stop talking about Xie Yan?

237
00:13:39,920 --> 00:13:41,480
He's the moon up in the sky,

238
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:44,600
while I'm just dirty water.

239
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:47,320
He has everything, and I have nothing,

240
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:52,520
so how can I not envy him?

241
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:01,480
Yes,

242
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:06,160
I got that letter dishonestly,

243
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:08,920
but it's still genuine.

244
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:10,760
With the official selection so close,

245
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:14,120
it's only a few more days of groveling.

246
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:17,280
I've already endured
thousands of days before this,

247
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:19,560
so why should now be any different?

248
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:23,280
I've come this far,

249
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,520
and I can't turn back,

250
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:28,200
or it will all have been for nothing.

251
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:36,080
Fine,

252
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:37,840
I understand.

253
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:41,240
There's something else

254
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:42,800
I came to ask you,

255
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:44,800
so please point me in the right direction.

256
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,720
The ledger is at the Lu residence.

257
00:14:54,200 --> 00:14:56,520
About the letter, I won't tell anyone.

258
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:06,920
Baozhu,

259
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:12,520
can you find it in your heart
to forgive me?

260
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:21,320
I understand you.

261
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:08,560
What a rare sight!

262
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:11,200
I never thought
we'd sit down for a drink together.

263
00:16:11,520 --> 00:16:12,600
That just shows

264
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:14,040
-what an extraordinary--
-Bai Junmei,

265
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:15,720
I need a favor from your father,

266
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:17,480
so arrange a meeting for me.

267
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:19,200
Chengjiang,

268
00:16:20,080 --> 00:16:21,560
this is a big favor,

269
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,680
not some little errand at the market!

270
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:27,240
-You'll have to--
-I'll put in a good word for you with Xi.

271
00:16:29,640 --> 00:16:31,960
-Cheers!
-If you do a good job.

272
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:35,400
Three orders of osmanthus cake

273
00:16:35,960 --> 00:16:37,600
and three plum drinks to go,

274
00:16:37,720 --> 00:16:39,240
all on Master Lu's tab.

275
00:16:43,520 --> 00:16:44,520
You've picked up bad habits,

276
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:47,360
eating here and taking food home, too!

277
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:53,120
Fill it up!

278
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Cheers!

279
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:01,120
Young Master Bai,

280
00:17:01,480 --> 00:17:03,920
I hear you need a favor.

281
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:06,560
Yes, yes. Thank you, Lord Lu,

282
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:08,520
for making time to see me today.

283
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:10,040
A toast to you both.

284
00:17:12,040 --> 00:17:13,040
Cheers.

285
00:17:27,840 --> 00:17:30,560
The shipping contract
is already set in stone.

286
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:32,920
Besides, I gave your family

287
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:34,680
the exam questions way back when,

288
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:36,160
so what can I do?

289
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:38,960
Yes, of course.

290
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:42,000
We're very grateful
for your help, Lord Lu.

291
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:43,680
A toast to you both.

292
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:47,240
Just tell me what you want.

293
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:49,600
One drink after another,
aren't you done yet?

294
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:53,600
No, it's just that…

295
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:57,080
with something like this,

296
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:58,840
I... I...

297
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:03,200
find it a little hard to ask.

298
00:18:03,840 --> 00:18:04,880
Give me a little time

299
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:07,960
and a couple of drinks to work up to it,

300
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:09,040
all right?

301
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:11,280
Come on.

302
00:18:12,160 --> 00:18:13,160
Cheers.

303
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,560
Father!

304
00:18:33,040 --> 00:18:34,040
Guards!

305
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:39,520
My lord.

306
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:43,520
Where's the hair?

307
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:45,360
My lord? What hair?

308
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:47,360
The hair I put inside this ledger,
where is it?

309
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:49,160
Has anyone been in here?

310
00:18:49,240 --> 00:18:51,360
My lord, I stood guard all night,

311
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:52,880
only leaving once to relieve myself.

312
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:55,000
Idiot! Get out!

313
00:18:55,160 --> 00:18:56,160
Yes, my lord!

314
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:02,720
Someone's touched this ledger.

315
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:06,960
Don't be angry, my lord.

316
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:09,080
At least the seal is real.

317
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:11,800
The intruder only flipped through it
for a second,

318
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:13,560
in the end,
they didn't get what they came for.

319
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:16,280
What could they be looking for in there?

320
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:18,160
Even if they saw anything,
they have no proof.

321
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:19,760
Besides, doesn't First Master Xie

322
00:19:19,880 --> 00:19:22,760
still have the second half?

323
00:19:23,800 --> 00:19:24,800
To be safe,

324
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:26,160
send him word.

325
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:31,360
Manyun!

326
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:34,280
Chanyue!

327
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,400
Good.

328
00:19:45,960 --> 00:19:46,960
Where's Manyun?

329
00:19:48,320 --> 00:19:49,600
She's still minding the shop,

330
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:50,680
so she isn't back yet,

331
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:52,800
and Mother's already asleep.

332
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:55,000
You're a grown man,

333
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:57,000
so why do something like this

334
00:19:57,320 --> 00:19:59,480
when a servant can do it?

335
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:02,960
It's too late to trouble them now.

336
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:05,400
We pay them,

337
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:07,880
so even in the middle of the night,

338
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:10,440
they can be put to work.

339
00:20:10,640 --> 00:20:12,160
Who have you been drinking with, Father,

340
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,400
to get this drunk?

341
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:17,040
Madam Shen will scold you if she hears.

342
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:19,800
A good friend,

343
00:20:20,120 --> 00:20:21,560
it's his birthday today.

344
00:20:22,440 --> 00:20:23,520
He's in high demand,

345
00:20:24,680 --> 00:20:27,360
and even though we'd planned
to go out for a drink,

346
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:29,120
he never showed,

347
00:20:30,240 --> 00:20:33,360
so I had a few extra cups on my own.

348
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:36,240
It's rare to see you so happy.

349
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:37,480
Let me tell you,

350
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:41,520
the salt shop business is sorted out,

351
00:20:42,640 --> 00:20:47,040
and Manyun is raking in money again.

352
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:48,440
Father.

353
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:50,880
Father,

354
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:52,280
have some soup to sober you up

355
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:54,360
while it's still hot.

356
00:21:18,640 --> 00:21:20,760
I'm your father,

357
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:23,040
and here I am,

358
00:21:23,680 --> 00:21:25,520
being waited on by you.

359
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:29,320
Heng, you resent me,

360
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:32,600
and I know it.

361
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:34,720
For as long as I can remember,

362
00:21:36,560 --> 00:21:39,200
you've left early and returned late,
working so hard.

363
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:41,080
Mother always said

364
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:44,320
your tireless work

365
00:21:45,040 --> 00:21:46,600
kept our family going,

366
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:48,640
so I've always been grateful

367
00:21:48,920 --> 00:21:52,840
and never forgotten it.

368
00:21:58,880 --> 00:22:01,640
It's just that sometimes,

369
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:06,200
the things you do
are hard for me to accept.

370
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:14,360
Why keep fighting it

371
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:16,200
when it's already done?

372
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:18,280
Come.

373
00:22:19,640 --> 00:22:20,640
Come here.

374
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:22,840
Come to your father.

375
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:28,440
I've always known you resent me,

376
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:30,800
and I'd rather you did

377
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:34,960
than have to watch you suffer.

378
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:39,240
Heng, in this life,

379
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:42,120
so much is beyond our control,

380
00:22:42,440 --> 00:22:43,840
and one day,

381
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:46,640
you'll understand.

382
00:22:47,960 --> 00:22:52,440
I know the road ahead is hard,

383
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:54,240
but rest assured,

384
00:22:55,800 --> 00:23:01,600
I will clear a smooth path for you,

385
00:23:02,160 --> 00:23:05,600
so all you need to do
is walk boldly forward.

386
00:23:08,360 --> 00:23:09,360
Keep going.

387
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:13,320
Father.

388
00:23:17,440 --> 00:23:18,440
Father.

389
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:38,960
You're very happy tonight.

390
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:42,360
I used to think life's greatest joy

391
00:23:42,440 --> 00:23:43,720
was passing the imperial exams,

392
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:44,840
then riding out in triumph.

393
00:23:45,640 --> 00:23:46,640
Now I find

394
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:50,200
holding her hand over warm tea

395
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:53,800
and chatting about our day is good, too.

396
00:23:58,760 --> 00:24:01,440
Tell me, are your legs any better?

397
00:24:05,720 --> 00:24:06,720
Much better.

398
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:11,080
Legs can heal, but a wounded heart
is harder to mend.

399
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:13,280
You were meant to triumph in the exams,

400
00:24:13,480 --> 00:24:14,920
so can you really be content

401
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:16,880
to settle quietly here?

402
00:24:21,240 --> 00:24:22,640
Then why don't you do it, Heng?

403
00:24:24,960 --> 00:24:28,640
You blame these legs for holding you back?

404
00:24:31,240 --> 00:24:32,400
I won't enter government service.

405
00:24:33,720 --> 00:24:35,400
I just don't understand

406
00:24:35,880 --> 00:24:37,240
why, now that your legs have healed

407
00:24:37,320 --> 00:24:38,520
and you have such talent,

408
00:24:39,240 --> 00:24:40,960
you won't clear your name and try again.

409
00:24:41,600 --> 00:24:43,240
Don't try to talk me into seeking office.

410
00:24:44,360 --> 00:24:45,640
Whatever I do,

411
00:24:45,960 --> 00:24:47,560
I always aim to be the best.

412
00:24:47,840 --> 00:24:50,520
Soon, I'll open a new shipping route

413
00:24:51,040 --> 00:24:53,040
without ever
taking any business from your family.

414
00:24:53,920 --> 00:24:55,040
It has nothing to do with that.

415
00:24:56,280 --> 00:24:57,560
I just can't understand

416
00:24:58,120 --> 00:24:59,400
why, when you're so gifted

417
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:01,160
and everything comes so easily to you,

418
00:25:01,720 --> 00:25:03,440
you won't achieve something great.

419
00:25:05,280 --> 00:25:08,680
What I love is worth achieving.

420
00:25:09,880 --> 00:25:11,440
If you have such grand ambitions,

421
00:25:12,160 --> 00:25:14,440
why pin your hopes on someone else

422
00:25:15,080 --> 00:25:16,440
instead of pursuing them yourself?

423
00:25:19,440 --> 00:25:22,720
I just think
the Xies have treated you well,

424
00:25:24,080 --> 00:25:25,640
so if you can help the family,

425
00:25:26,840 --> 00:25:27,880
why wouldn't you?

426
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:30,160
As it happens,

427
00:25:31,280 --> 00:25:32,320
there is something

428
00:25:33,080 --> 00:25:34,600
I'd like your help with.

429
00:25:36,680 --> 00:25:37,680
Me?

430
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:40,160
Something

431
00:25:41,360 --> 00:25:42,880
that concerns the whole family's safety.

432
00:26:07,360 --> 00:26:09,520
It's the wrong path that's hard, Father.

433
00:26:25,160 --> 00:26:26,520
Uncle and Lu Xian go back a long way,

434
00:26:26,680 --> 00:26:28,160
with money changing hands between them

435
00:26:28,240 --> 00:26:29,640
as they do each other favors.

436
00:26:30,480 --> 00:26:32,760
The news about salt prices
came from the officials,

437
00:26:32,920 --> 00:26:34,560
which is why they were so sure.

438
00:26:50,520 --> 00:26:53,960
If this comes to light,

439
00:26:54,440 --> 00:26:58,480
could you spare him,

440
00:27:07,240 --> 00:27:08,760
spare my father's life?

441
00:27:19,120 --> 00:27:22,320
I thought you'd be angry to hear that.

442
00:27:23,440 --> 00:27:24,520
Not anymore.

443
00:27:25,040 --> 00:27:26,240
I've been thinking.

444
00:27:27,200 --> 00:27:28,240
Go on, wise one.

445
00:27:28,640 --> 00:27:30,440
Life isn't a game of Go,

446
00:27:30,680 --> 00:27:31,760
it's not just black and white.

447
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:35,600
You have to put…

448
00:27:35,680 --> 00:27:36,720
Put your…

449
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:40,800
Put yourself in someone else's shoes,

450
00:27:40,880 --> 00:27:42,840
then think it through before you decide.

451
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:47,080
So you've gone soft?

452
00:27:49,920 --> 00:27:51,000
I can understand,

453
00:27:51,160 --> 00:27:52,440
but that doesn't mean I can forgive.

454
00:27:52,920 --> 00:27:55,120
Wrongdoing must be dealt with fairly.

455
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:00,600
Heng is usually so tight-lipped,

456
00:28:00,840 --> 00:28:02,200
but seeing him like that,

457
00:28:03,280 --> 00:28:04,800
I almost wanted to say yes,

458
00:28:06,720 --> 00:28:09,160
though there's still something important
we have to do.

459
00:28:09,640 --> 00:28:10,640
What?

460
00:28:13,280 --> 00:28:14,280
Pay up.

461
00:28:14,800 --> 00:28:16,440
How about a shovel to the head?

462
00:28:17,280 --> 00:28:18,800
Look who's talking!

463
00:28:19,160 --> 00:28:20,560
Yesterday, to cover for you two,

464
00:28:20,640 --> 00:28:22,600
I drank so much I was throwing up bile,

465
00:28:23,200 --> 00:28:24,480
not to mention offending an official.

466
00:28:24,560 --> 00:28:25,680
So what's wrong with
a little compensation?

467
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:30,360
For us, or to protect your own money?

468
00:28:30,880 --> 00:28:32,840
Besides,
your family's so rich and powerful,

469
00:28:32,920 --> 00:28:34,680
you're hardly afraid
of being taken down with them.

470
00:28:35,800 --> 00:28:37,000
You could at least pay something

471
00:28:37,320 --> 00:28:38,960
toward buying back the salt permits.

472
00:28:40,040 --> 00:28:42,280
Wait a little longer,
and you'll get your money.

473
00:28:45,800 --> 00:28:47,440
Come and see these trinkets!

474
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:50,200
Your business doesn't look too good.

475
00:28:50,600 --> 00:28:54,560
I hear a new shop just opened
at the entrance to this alley,

476
00:28:54,960 --> 00:28:57,120
they copied your whole way of making stew,

477
00:28:57,240 --> 00:28:58,480
and they're cheaper, too.

478
00:28:58,720 --> 00:29:00,520
How do you expect to stay in business,

479
00:29:00,600 --> 00:29:02,360
let alone pay me back?

480
00:29:03,080 --> 00:29:04,120
What's the hurry?

481
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:05,560
I have a plan.

482
00:29:05,920 --> 00:29:07,960
If I were you, I'd be happy to wait

483
00:29:08,040 --> 00:29:09,560
and collect more interest.

484
00:29:09,640 --> 00:29:13,160
Besides, the Xie family isn't
going anywhere, is it?

485
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:18,160
Yangzhou docks

486
00:29:18,240 --> 00:29:19,920
-Don't push! Don't push!
-Here, take this.

487
00:29:20,720 --> 00:29:22,280
Don't push! There's enough for everyone!

488
00:29:22,360 --> 00:29:23,360
-Zhang Afu, right?
-Yes, that's me.

489
00:29:23,440 --> 00:29:25,440
-Here you are.
-Got it. Thank you!

490
00:29:26,440 --> 00:29:27,440
-Don't push!
-Here's yours.

491
00:29:27,760 --> 00:29:28,760
-There's enough for everyone!
-Thank you!

492
00:29:28,840 --> 00:29:29,920
-Here.
-Thank you!

493
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:31,560
If we'd known how generous he was,

494
00:29:31,640 --> 00:29:32,880
-we'd have found shipping contracts, too.
-Here's yours.

495
00:29:32,960 --> 00:29:35,440
-Work more, earn more. Got it?
-Here you are.

496
00:29:35,560 --> 00:29:36,560
-Yes!
-Yes!

497
00:29:37,320 --> 00:29:38,960
What I promised you,

498
00:29:39,040 --> 00:29:41,080
your share of the shipping profits
and the proceeds from the spices,

499
00:29:41,240 --> 00:29:42,480
has all been paid out now.

500
00:29:43,280 --> 00:29:44,280
It's been a busy time,

501
00:29:45,520 --> 00:29:46,520
so thank you for all your hard work.

502
00:29:46,680 --> 00:29:49,120
-Thank you, young master!
-Thank you, young master!

503
00:29:49,200 --> 00:29:51,640
You're setting sail today
without the young master,

504
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:53,360
so please take extra care.

505
00:29:53,440 --> 00:29:55,200
Same as before, 20% of the profits.

506
00:29:55,280 --> 00:29:57,400
Work more, earn more,
work less, earn less.

507
00:29:57,480 --> 00:29:59,320
You'll be rewarded when you return!

508
00:29:59,440 --> 00:30:01,040
-Yes! Yes!
-Yes! Yes!

509
00:30:01,120 --> 00:30:02,240
-Come on, all aboard!
-Yes!

510
00:30:02,320 --> 00:30:03,320
Young master.

511
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Thank you for your hard work.

512
00:30:06,640 --> 00:30:07,640
Have a safe journey.

513
00:30:08,040 --> 00:30:09,360
Rest assured, young master,

514
00:30:09,440 --> 00:30:10,640
everything's been arranged.

515
00:30:10,720 --> 00:30:13,680
You should head back
before it starts raining.

516
00:30:15,360 --> 00:30:17,560
-Come on!
-Hurry!

517
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:25,320
Xie

518
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:53,640
Guess who?

519
00:30:54,640 --> 00:30:55,640
Xie Yan.

520
00:30:59,360 --> 00:31:01,040
Didn't you leave?

521
00:31:09,560 --> 00:31:10,560
Didn't quite make it.

522
00:31:11,280 --> 00:31:12,280
-Miss me--
-My lady,

523
00:31:12,640 --> 00:31:15,400
Grandmother's furious
and wants us there right away.
